<section class="legacy-workspace" id="about_workspace" aria-labelledby="about_title">
  <header class="legacy-workspace-header">
    <div>
      <p class="legacy-workspace-eyebrow">Project</p>
      <h1 id="about_title">About Orchestrator</h1>
      <p>High availability, replication management, and topology visibility for MySQL and PostgreSQL.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-outline-light" href="https://github.com/ProxySQL/orchestrator" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on GitHub</a>
  </header>

  <div class="legacy-workspace-grid legacy-workspace-grid--about">
    <article class="legacy-panel legacy-panel--lead">
      <span class="legacy-kicker">Current database support</span>
      <h2>One operational view across modern database fleets</h2>
      <p>Orchestrator discovers replication topologies, identifies failures, supports controlled topology changes, and can coordinate automated recovery.</p>
      <div class="legacy-support-grid">
        <div>
          <strong>MySQL</strong>
          <span>Current releases through MySQL 9.7, including the 8.4 LTS line.</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>PostgreSQL</strong>
          <span>PostgreSQL 12 and newer, with discovery, failure detection, and failover support.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="legacy-panel">
      <span class="legacy-kicker">What it provides</span>
      <ul class="legacy-feature-list">
        <li><strong>Discover</strong><span>Continuously map replication relationships and instance health.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Visualize</strong><span>Explore clusters, replicas, problems, maintenance, and recovery state.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Recover</strong><span>Analyze failures and coordinate manual or automated topology recovery.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Audit</strong><span>Review topology operations, failure detections, and recovery history.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="legacy-panel legacy-panel--project">
      <span class="legacy-kicker">Open source</span>
      <h2>Maintained by ProxySQL</h2>
      <p>The project is maintained at <a href="https://github.com/ProxySQL/orchestrator" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ProxySQL/orchestrator</a> and welcomes issues and contributions from the community.</p>
      <p>Orchestrator is distributed under the <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apache License 2.0</a>.</p>
      <div class="legacy-link-row">
        <a href="https://proxysql.github.io/orchestrator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Documentation</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/ProxySQL/orchestrator/blob/master/docs/faq.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAQ</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/ProxySQL/orchestrator/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Releases</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <p id="customized" class="legacy-workspace-note" style="display: none">This installation includes local UI customizations.</p>
</section>

<script type="text/javascript">
  $.get('../css/custom.css', function(content) {
    if (content.length > 0) $('#customized').show();
  });
  $.get('../js/custom.js', function(content) {
    if (content.length > 0) $('#customized').show();
  });
</script>
